---
title: Com Sign-Up State Machine
---

%% Partially superseded by Identity Authority inversion.
%% sign/id is ceremony-only; acme/www commits account and session state.

%% Current runtime vocabulary. Future canonical lifecycle terminology is defined in
%% docs/security/idp-flow-lifecycle.md and is not implemented yet.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> STARTED: begin sign-up cycle
  STARTED --> IDENTITY_PENDING: select or receive identity strategy

  note right of IDENTITY_PENDING
    Provider and entry details are strategy data,
    not lifecycle state: email, telephone, gift,
    invitation, or future public-surface methods.
  end note

  IDENTITY_PENDING --> identity_route: identity accepted
  IDENTITY_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable identity failure

  state identity_route <<choice>>
  identity_route --> CONTACT_PENDING: contact verification required
  identity_route --> CREDENTIAL_PENDING: credential setup required
  identity_route --> GUARDRAIL_PENDING: identity requirements already satisfied

  CONTACT_PENDING --> contact_route: contact verified
  CONTACT_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable contact failure

  state contact_route <<choice>>
  contact_route --> CREDENTIAL_PENDING: credential setup required
  contact_route --> GUARDRAIL_PENDING: credential already satisfied

  CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> GUARDRAIL_PENDING: credential registered
  CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable credential failure

  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> CHECKPOINT_PENDING: guardrail cleared
  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> FAILED: guardrail blocks continuation

  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> FINALIZING: required checkpoint items cleared
  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable checkpoint failure

  FINALIZING --> SIGN_IN_HANDOFF_PENDING: account artifacts committed
  FINALIZING --> FAILED: commit failed or integrity check failed

  SIGN_IN_HANDOFF_PENDING --> COMPLETED: sign-in handoff accepted
  SIGN_IN_HANDOFF_PENDING --> FAILED: handoff failed before completion

  STARTED --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  IDENTITY_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  CONTACT_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels

  STARTED --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  IDENTITY_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  CONTACT_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires

  note right of FAILED
    FAILED means unrecoverable, non-resumable cycle
    failure. Retryable validation errors do not enter
    this terminal state.
  end note

  note right of EXPIRED
    EXPIRED, FAILED, and CANCELLED require retention
    scheduling and artifact cleanup. COMPLETED does not.
  end note

  COMPLETED --> [*]
  EXPIRED --> [*]
  FAILED --> [*]
  CANCELLED --> [*]
